        "C_mean_error": "<= 1.0 mm",
        "C_corr": ">= 0.98"
      },
      "notes": [
        "C localises the contact as the depth-weighted centroid of the taxel map. A is one bit per fingertip, so it carries no location. B is a net force vector, but in this noiseless set-up a linear map of it recovers the across-pad position almost perfectly and the along-pad position only partly (B_linear_fit_R2): the pad is a curved capsule, so the force direction depends on where it is pressed across it. That is not a reliable location sensor on a real contact patch or under noise, and B cannot separate two contacts (T4) while C can."
      ]
